  "name": "Social Mobility Policy Committee",
  "parent_committee_id": null,
  "purpose": "<p>The Social Mobility Policy Committee was appointed to consider how educational and work opportunities could be better integrated to improve social mobility in the UK.</p>\r\n<p>Follow the Committee on <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/hlsocmobility.parliament.uk\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/social-mobility-policy-committee/\">LinkedIn</a>, or <a href=\"https://x.com/HLSocMobility\">X (formerly Twitter)</a>.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://ukparliament.shorthandstories.com/social-mobility-policy-lords-report/index.html?utm_source=committees.parliament.uk&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=social-mobility-policy-report&amp;utm_content=inquiry-page-banner\">Read the key points in our report summary</a></p>\r\n<p>The report <a href=\"https://publications.parliament.uk/pa/ld5901/ldselect/ldsocmob/201/201.pdf\">Social Mobility: Local Roots, Lasting Change</a>&nbsp;was published 18 November 2025, the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/social-mobility-local-roots-lasting-change-government-response\">Government Response</a>&nbsp;was published 24 July 2026 and the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://hansard.parliament.uk/lords/2026-09-04/debates/C7926559-5B62-4E23-97B1-0F2311A0E4AD/SocialMobilityLocalRootsLastingChange(SocialMobilityPolicyCommitteeReport)\">report was debated</a>&nbsp;4 September 2026.</p>",
